{"authored" [] "sources" [{"question" "q-64288" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find the Laplace transform $L{{f}^{″}(t)}$ for $s>0,$ given that the function $f(t)$ is continuous on $[0,\\infty ),$ ${f}^{′}(0)=-1,$ $f(0)=1,$ and\n\n$$\nL{f(t)}=\\frac{s-1}{{s}^{2}+1},\\,s>0.\n$$\n\nAssume that ${f}^{′}$ is continuous and ${f}^{″}$ piecewise continuous on $[0,\\infty ).$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14070484/state.json" "file_sha256" "b7d191b83f45f3792635dfda30e6399a8dcb785c271a5d462d0f9a3bd5dfe565"} {"question" "q-64288" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Suppose $F(s)=L{f(t)}$ where $f(t)$ is a continuous function of exponential order $a$ on $[0,\\infty ).$ If ${f}^{′}(t)$ is continuous and ${f}^{″}(t)$ is piecewise continuous on $[0,\\infty ),$ then\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L{{f}^{″}(t)} & ={s}^{2}L{f(t)}-sf(0)-{f}^{′}(0).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we can calculate the Laplace transform of ${f}^{″}(t)$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L{{f}^{″}(t)} & ={s}^{2}\\cdot \\frac{s-1}{{s}^{2}+1}-s\\cdot 1-(-1) \\\\  & =\\frac{{s}^{2}(s-1)}{{s}^{2}+1}-s+1 \\\\  & =\\frac{{s}^{2}(s-1)}{{s}^{2}+1}-(s-1) \\\\  & =(s-1)(\\frac{{s}^{2}}{{s}^{2}+1}-1) \\\\  & =(s-1)(-\\frac{1}{{s}^{2}+1}) \\\\  & =\\frac{1-s}{{s}^{2}+1}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nvalid for $s>0.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14070484/state.json" "file_sha256" "b7d191b83f45f3792635dfda30e6399a8dcb785c271a5d462d0f9a3bd5dfe565"} {"question" "q-64288" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14070484/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "b48c735e0f7bb5f27ddb466abbec4ef1cc7b3e126e604367c55e480c371f4091"} {"question" "q-64288" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14070484/state.json" "file_sha256" "b7d191b83f45f3792635dfda30e6399a8dcb785c271a5d462d0f9a3bd5dfe565"} {"question" "q-64288" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "\\frac{1-s}{{s}^{2}+1}"] ["math" "\\frac{1}{s({s}^{2}+1)}"] ["math" "\\frac{2-s}{s({s}^{2}+1)}"] ["math" "\\frac{s+2}{{s}^{2}+1}"] ["math" "\\frac{s}{{s}^{2}+1}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14070484/state.json" "file_sha256" "b7d191b83f45f3792635dfda30e6399a8dcb785c271a5d462d0f9a3bd5dfe565"} {"question" "q-64288" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{1-s}{{s}^{2}+1}"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14070484/state.json" "file_sha256" "b7d191b83f45f3792635dfda30e6399a8dcb785c271a5d462d0f9a3bd5dfe565"} {"question" "q-64325" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find the Laplace transform of ${f}^{′}(t)$ for $s>4$ given that the function $f(t)$ is continuous over $[0,\\infty ),$ $f(0)=1,$ and\n\n$$\nL{f(t)}=\\frac{s-4}{{s}^{2}-8s+20},\\,s>4.\n$$\n\nAssume that ${f}^{′}$ is piecewise continuous on $[0,\\infty ).$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14070484/state.json" "file_sha256" "b7d191b83f45f3792635dfda30e6399a8dcb785c271a5d462d0f9a3bd5dfe565"} {"question" "q-64325" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Suppose $F(s)=L{f(t)}$ where $f(t)$ is a continuous function of exponential order $a$ on $[0,\\infty ).$ If ${f}^{′}(t)$ is piecewise continuous on $[0,\\infty ),$ then\n\n$$\nL{{f}^{′}(t)}=sL{f(t)}-f(0).\n$$\n\nTherefore, we can calculate the Laplace transform of ${f}^{′}(t)$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L{{f}^{′}(t)} & =sL{f(t)}-f(0) \\\\  & =s\\cdot \\frac{s-4}{{s}^{2}-8s+20}-1 \\\\  & =\\frac{s(s-4)-({s}^{2}-8s+20)}{{s}^{2}-8s+20} \\\\  & =\\frac{4s-20}{{s}^{2}-8s+20}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nvalid for $s>4.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14070484/state.json" "file_sha256" "b7d191b83f45f3792635dfda30e6399a8dcb785c271a5d462d0f9a3bd5dfe565"} {"question" "q-64325" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14070484/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "b48c735e0f7bb5f27ddb466abbec4ef1cc7b3e126e604367c55e480c371f4091"} {"question" "q-64325" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14070484/state.json" "file_sha256" "b7d191b83f45f3792635dfda30e6399a8dcb785c271a5d462d0f9a3bd5dfe565"} {"question" "q-64325" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "\\frac{2s-16}{{s}^{2}-8s+20}"] ["math" "\\frac{4s-20}{{s}^{2}-8s+20}"] ["math" "\\frac{s-4}{{s}^{2}-8s+20}"] ["math" "\\frac{{s}^{2}+s+16}{{s}^{2}-8s+20}"] ["math" "\\frac{{s}^{2}-20}{{s}^{2}-8s+20}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14070484/state.json" "file_sha256" "b7d191b83f45f3792635dfda30e6399a8dcb785c271a5d462d0f9a3bd5dfe565"} {"question" "q-64325" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{4s-20}{{s}^{2}-8s+20}"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14070484/state.json" "file_sha256" "b7d191b83f45f3792635dfda30e6399a8dcb785c271a5d462d0f9a3bd5dfe565"} {"question" "q-89450" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find the Laplace transform of ${f}^{′}(t)$ for $s>3$ given that the function $f(t)$ is continuous over $[0,\\infty ),$ $f(0)=5,$ and\n\n$$\nL{f(t)}=\\frac{5s-6}{{s}^{2}-3s},\\,s>3.\n$$\n\nAssume that ${f}^{′}$ is piecewise continuous on $[0,\\infty ).$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14070484/state.json" "file_sha256" "b7d191b83f45f3792635dfda30e6399a8dcb785c271a5d462d0f9a3bd5dfe565"} {"question" "q-89450" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Suppose $F(s)=L{f(t)}$ where $f(t)$ is a continuous function of exponential order $a$ on $[0,\\infty ).$ If ${f}^{′}(t)$ is piecewise continuous on $[0,\\infty ),$ then\n\n$$\nL{{f}^{′}(t)}=sL{f(t)}-f(0).\n$$\n\nTherefore, we can calculate the Laplace transform of ${f}^{′}(t)$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L{{f}^{′}(t)} & =sL{f(t)}-f(0) \\\\  & =s\\cdot \\frac{5s-6}{{s}^{2}-3s}-5 \\\\  & =\\frac{5{s}^{2}-6s}{{s}^{2}-3s}-5 \\\\  & =\\frac{9s}{{s}^{2}-3s} \\\\  & =\\frac{9s}{s(s-3)} \\\\  & =\\frac{9}{s-3}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nvalid for $s>3.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14070484/state.json" "file_sha256" "b7d191b83f45f3792635dfda30e6399a8dcb785c271a5d462d0f9a3bd5dfe565"} {"question" "q-89450" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14070484/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "b48c735e0f7bb5f27ddb466abbec4ef1cc7b3e126e604367c55e480c371f4091"} {"question" "q-89450" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14070484/state.json" "file_sha256" "b7d191b83f45f3792635dfda30e6399a8dcb785c271a5d462d0f9a3bd5dfe565"} {"question" "q-89450" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "\\frac{2s-1}{s-3}"] ["math" "\\frac{3s}{s-3}"] ["math" "\\frac{5}{s-3}"] ["math" "\\frac{9}{s-3}"] ["math" "\\frac{s}{s-3}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14070484/state.json" "file_sha256" "b7d191b83f45f3792635dfda30e6399a8dcb785c271a5d462d0f9a3bd5dfe565"} {"question" "q-89450" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{9}{s-3}"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14070484/state.json" "file_sha256" "b7d191b83f45f3792635dfda30e6399a8dcb785c271a5d462d0f9a3bd5dfe565"} {"question" "q-89462" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find the Laplace transform $L{{f}^{″}(t)}$ for $s>0,$ given that the function $f(t)$ is continuous on $[0,\\infty ),$ ${f}^{′}(0)=3,$ $f(0)=-1,$ and\n\n$$\nL{f(t)}=\\frac{3-s}{{s}^{2}+9},\\,s>0.\n$$\n\nAssume that ${f}^{′}$ is continuous and ${f}^{″}$ piecewise continuous on $[0,\\infty ).$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14070484/state.json" "file_sha256" "b7d191b83f45f3792635dfda30e6399a8dcb785c271a5d462d0f9a3bd5dfe565"} {"question" "q-89462" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Suppose $F(s)=L{f(t)}$ where $f(t)$ is a continuous function of exponential order $a$ on $[0,\\infty ).$ If ${f}^{′}(t)$ is continuous and ${f}^{″}(t)$ is piecewise continuous on $[0,\\infty ),$ then\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L{{f}^{″}(t)} & ={s}^{2}L{f(t)}-sf(0)-{f}^{′}(0).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we can calculate the Laplace transform of ${f}^{″}(t)$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L{{f}^{″}(t)} & ={s}^{2}\\cdot \\frac{3-s}{{s}^{2}+9}-s\\cdot (-1)-3 \\\\  & =\\frac{{s}^{2}(3-s)}{{s}^{2}+9}+s-3 \\\\  & =\\frac{(s-3)({s}^{2}+9-{s}^{2})}{{s}^{2}+9} \\\\  & =\\frac{9s-27}{{s}^{2}+9}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nvalid for $s>0.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14070484/state.json" "file_sha256" "b7d191b83f45f3792635dfda30e6399a8dcb785c271a5d462d0f9a3bd5dfe565"} {"question" "q-89462" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14070484/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "b48c735e0f7bb5f27ddb466abbec4ef1cc7b3e126e604367c55e480c371f4091"} {"question" "q-89462" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14070484/state.json" "file_sha256" "b7d191b83f45f3792635dfda30e6399a8dcb785c271a5d462d0f9a3bd5dfe565"} {"question" "q-89462" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "\\frac{27}{{s}^{2}+9}"] ["math" "\\frac{3s}{{s}^{2}+9}"] ["math" "\\frac{9s-27}{{s}^{2}+9}"] ["math" "\\frac{9s}{{s}^{2}+9}"] ["math" "\\frac{{s}^{2}-3}{{s}^{2}+9}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14070484/state.json" "file_sha256" "b7d191b83f45f3792635dfda30e6399a8dcb785c271a5d462d0f9a3bd5dfe565"} {"question" "q-89462" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{9s-27}{{s}^{2}+9}"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14070484/state.json" "file_sha256" "b7d191b83f45f3792635dfda30e6399a8dcb785c271a5d462d0f9a3bd5dfe565"} {"question" "q-341395" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find the Laplace transform $L{{f}^{″}(t)}$ for $s>1,$ given that the function $f(t)$ is continuous on $[0,\\infty ),$ ${f}^{′}(0)=-1,$ $f(0)=5,$ and\n\n$$\nL{f(t)}=\\frac{5s+4}{(s-1)(s+2)},\\,s>1.\n$$\n\nAssume that ${f}^{′}$ is continuous and ${f}^{″}$ piecewise continuous on $[0,\\infty ).$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14070484/state.json" "file_sha256" "b7d191b83f45f3792635dfda30e6399a8dcb785c271a5d462d0f9a3bd5dfe565"} {"question" "q-341395" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Suppose $F(s)=L{f(t)}$ where $f(t)$ is a continuous function of exponential order $a$ on $[0,\\infty ).$ If ${f}^{′}(t)$ is continuous and ${f}^{″}(t)$ is piecewise continuous on $[0,\\infty ),$ then\n\n$$\nL{{f}^{″}(t)}={s}^{2}L{f(t)}-sf(0)-{f}^{′}(0).\n$$\n\nTherefore, we can calculate the Laplace transform of ${f}^{″}(t)$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L{{f}^{″}(t)} & ={s}^{2}\\cdot \\frac{5s+4}{(s-1)(s+2)}-s\\cdot 5-(-1) \\\\  & ={s}^{2}\\cdot \\frac{5s+4}{(s-1)(s+2)}-(5s-1) \\\\  & =\\frac{{s}^{2}(5s+4)-(5s-1)(s-1)(s+2)}{(s-1)(s+2)} \\\\  & =\\frac{5{s}^{3}+4{s}^{2}-(5{s}^{3}+4{s}^{2}-11s+2)}{(s-1)(s+2)} \\\\  & =\\frac{11s-2}{(s-1)(s+2)}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nvalid for $s>1.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14070484/state.json" "file_sha256" "b7d191b83f45f3792635dfda30e6399a8dcb785c271a5d462d0f9a3bd5dfe565"} {"question" "q-341395" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Develope